{"tool": "finish", "summary": "Added an `audit_log` table and made every API request that modifies `users` or `feeds` append a row to it. The build and existing tests pass (53 unit packages, 102 integration tests); the audit behaviour itself has no test of its own.\n\n**Schema** (new migration): `audit_log(id, created_at, user_id, action, table_name, row_id)`. `user_id` is the requesting user and is deliberately not a foreign key, so rows survive user deletion. `row_id` is NULL when a request touches several rows.\n\n**REST API (`/v1`)** \u2014 audited requests:\n- Users: create, update, delete.\n- Feeds: create, update, delete, refresh of a single feed.\n- OPML import: one row per feed created.\n- Category delete: one row per feed removed by the cascade.\n- Refresh all feeds / refresh a category: one row per request when at least one feed is queued.\n\n**Google Reader API**: subscribe, quick-add, unsubscribe, rename, move, and disable-tag are audited too. I treated it as an API in scope; say if you want it limited to `/v1`.\n\nLast-login updates in the auth middleware are not audited, as specified.\n\nThings you might trip over:\n- The audit row is written right after the modification, not in the same transaction. If the audit insert fails the request returns 500, but the modification has already happened.\n- A single-feed refresh is audited even when the refresh fails, because failures still update the feed's error counter and next-check time.\n- The background refresh requests are audited at request time, before the worker actually updates the feeds.\n- Disable-tag writes one row even if the removed categories held no feeds.\n- A `/v1` feed creation or Google Reader subscribe that fails after the feed row was inserted leaves that row unaudited.\n\nSupporting changes: `opml.Handler.Import` now takes optional per-feed callbacks (existing callers unchanged), new storage methods `CreateAuditLog` and `CategoryFeedIDs`, `audit_log` added to the `.agentpolicy` nouns for `storage`, `api` and `googlereader`, and `@effects` tags ", "t": 1794462374.658}
{"tool": "_result", "name": "finish", "chars": 55, "t": 1794462374.659}
